<h1>Melissa Conyears-Ervin</h1>
<p>City Treasurer, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027. Incumbent.</p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Politico&#39;s Illinois Playbook reported in August 2026 that she is running for a third term as treasurer after her unsuccessful 2026 congressional bid. No campaign website or detailed platform for the treasurer race found yet. In August 2026 she urged the City Council to dissolve the Chicago Community Catalyst Fund and move its more than $57 million into the city&#39;s corporate fund, saying the money should help avoid police and firefighter layoffs.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Chicago City Treasurer since 2019; Illinois state representative for the 10th District from 2017 to 2019; earlier spent 15 years as an executive at Allstate Insurance.</p>
